                            <comment id="497408" author="JIRAUSER18021" created="Tue, 7 Jul 2026 19:50:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;There is &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20308&quot; title=&quot;sanity-lfsck test_0: el10.1: FAIL: (10) Expect nothing to be repaired, but got: 98&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20308&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20308&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 2.18 blocker and I believe that it has the same root cause&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="498132" author="JIRAUSER18021" created="Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:52:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;AI bot pointed to a problem&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&quot;Some concerns, see inline comments. The same ext4_htree_store_dirent dirdata fix is missing from linux-6.18/ext4-dirdata-core.patch, which ldiskfs-6.18-ml, ldiskfs-7.0-ml and ldiskfs-7.0.0-14-ubuntu26 all apply; those kernels still drop the FID from hash-ordered readdir and hit the same osd_fid_unpack() error. Was leaving them out of this patch intentional, or should the hunk be added there too?&quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;, but I fixed only series from original patch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=stancheff&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;stancheff&quot;&gt;stancheff&lt;/a&gt; , you ported these series and probably have these environments ready. Could you please port this patch there too? Thanks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
